From 23eb439dbc5fc1f7a57cdf907ba0934c95934915 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:07:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: ktz8869_iceland: make the vddio supply optional

The OnePlus Pad 4 drives the HWEN pin of both KTZ8869 from a GPIO and
feeds their VDDIO from an always-on rail; neither the board's device
tree nor the vendor one describes a supply for it, so every probe
printed "supply vddio not found, using dummy regulator".

Request vddio as an optional supply and only fail on real errors.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c b/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c
index f6dd2c61a6..d1196bd030 100644
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c
@@ -183,8 +183,12 @@ static int ktz8869_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	ret = devm_regulator_get_enable(&client->dev, "vin");
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(&client->dev, ret, "get regulator vin failed\n");
-	ret = devm_regulator_get_enable(&client->dev, "vddio");
-	if (ret)
+	/*
+	 * Boards that drive the HWEN pin from a GPIO feed VDDIO from an
+	 * always-on rail and describe no supply for it.
+	 */
+	ret = devm_regulator_get_enable_optional(&client->dev, "vddio");
+	if (ret && ret != -ENODEV)
 		return dev_err_probe(&client->dev, ret, "get regulator vddio failed\n");
 
 	if (id->driver_data == 2) {
-- 
